<span id="S4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.7em;">
<span id="S4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Does the RICH Explain Test-Time Scaling’s Effects on Attack-Bard Classification?<span id="S4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Yes, scaling test-compute via CoT improves robustness on Attack-Bard data per the RICH.</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
